sao raimundo rr -> ['Sao Raimundo RR']\nsuzano sp -> ['Suzano SP']\ntombense mg -> ['Tombense MG']\ntrem ap -> ['Trem AP']\ntupi mg -> ['Tupi MG']\nuniclinic ce -> ['Uniclinic CE']\nurt mg -> ['URT MG']\nvilhena ro -> ['Vilhena RO']\nypiranga ap -> ['Ypiranga AP']\nypiranga rs -> ['Ypiranga RS']\n","exit":0,"description":"Find teams with unstripped state suffix causing mismatch","truncated":false},"title":"Find teams with unstripped state suffix causing mismatch","time":{"start":1782087402817,"end":1782087402863}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found it! The dates differ slightly between sources for the SAME fixture:\n- cruzeiro: brfootball 2019-04-28 vs brasileirao 2019-04-27 (off by 1 day)\n- internacional: brfootball 2019-09-26 vs brasileirao 2019-09-25\n- atletico_mg: brfootball 2019-10-11 vs brasileirao 2019-10-10\n- csa: brfootball \"csa\" vs brasileirao \"csa al\" — DIFFERENT away_id! \"csa al\" is the fallback (brasileirao source has \"CSA-AL\" → _clean \"csa al\" → fallback \"csa al\"), while brfootball has \"CSA\" → _clean \"csa\" → fallback \"csa\". So canonical ids differ (\"csa\" vs \"csa al\")! Team name normalization bug for CSA.\n\nAlso corinthians, vasco, ceara dates differ by 1-2 days.\n\nSo two problems:\n1. Dates off by 1 day between sources → dedup by date fails.\n2. Team canonical id mismatches for some clubs (CSA, Ceara, etc.) across sources.\n\nFor (2): brasileirao has \"CSA-AL\" (CSA from Alagoas) and brfootball has \"CSA\". I need to canonicalize both to \"csa\". Similarly \"Ceara-CE\" (brasileirao) vs \"Ceara\" (brfootball) — wait \"Ceara\" is a club (Ceará Sporting). \"ceara\" canonical. brasileirao \"Ceará-CE\"? Let me check — brasileirao home sample didn't show Ceara but away showed \"Ceara CE\"? The Flamengo brasileirao list shows \"ceara ce\" for away_id? No — it shows away_id \"ceara ce\"? The output shows `3004  2019-11-27       ceara ce` — yes \"ceara ce\" (brasileirao \"Ceará-CE\" → _clean \"ceara ce\" → fallback \"ceara ce\"). And brfootball \"Ceara\" → \"ceara\". Mismatch!\n\nSo my normalizer needs to handle these. The issue: fallback keeps the state token. For teams like CSA, Ceara, Fortaleza, Bahia, etc. that are named after their state, the state suffix causes mismatches between sources that include/exclude it.\n\nI need a broader alias set. Let me add more aliases for Brazilian clubs that appear in both brasileirao and brfootball. Let me extract the teams that appear in Brasileirao (Serie A level, 2012-2022) and cross-reference with brfootball team names, and find mismatches.\n\nActually, a cleaner general fix: in the FALLBACK, also strip a trailing state code IF the resulting base, when looked up, would be unambiguous. But the simplest: build the alias map from the data by linking teams across sources via the round+season+opponent. That's complex.\n\nPragmatic approach: Expand the curated alias map to cover all clubs that appear in the Brasileirao Serie A (top division) datasets, since those are the ones that matter for standings/champion queries. Let me extract unique clubs from Brasileirao_Matches (home_team) and map each to a canonical id, ensuring brfootball spellings map to the same.\n\nLet me get the list of Brasileirao clubs (from both brasileirao and hist and brfootball Serie A) and build a comprehensive alias map. Let me extract and curate.\n\nActually, let me take a different, more robust dedup approach that doesn't rely on perfect date matching AND handles team name variations:\n\nFor dedup, use key (competition, season, home_id, away_id) WITHOUT date, but to handle the Libertadores group+knockout same-ordered-pair case, I can additionally use `round` when available, else date. But brfootball has no round. Hmm.\n\nActually for the Brasileirao/Serie B/Serie C league (the ones with standings), dropping date and deduping by (competition, season, home_id, away_id) is SAFE because it's a pure double round-robin: each ordered pair meets exactly once per season. The date differences won't matter. And team-name mismatches (CSA vs csa al) I'll fix via the alias map. Let me verify: does the Brasileirao dataset have any case where the same ordered pair meets twice in a season? No, double round-robin = each ordered pair once. Good. So for league competitions, dedup by (competition, season, home_id, away_id) is safe and robust.\n\nFor Copa do Brasil and Libertadores (knockout), the same ordered pair could appear twice? In Copa do Brasil, a tie is two legs with reversed home/away, so ordered pairs differ. But could the same ordered pair recur across different rounds (e.g., a team hosts opponent in round 1, then again in final)? Extremely unlikely. So (competition, season, home_id, away_id) is also safe for cups in practice. But to be safe for the Libertadores group+knockout same-pair case, including date would help — but date mismatches across sources hurt. Trade-off.\n\nGiven the benchmark focuses on Brazilian clubs and the standings example, the league dedup is the critical one. Let me dedup by (competition, season, home_id, away_id) — dropping date. This handles date mismatches. The risk of merging two distinct same-pair matches in a season is negligible for these datasets. I'll accept it.\n\nBut I also need to fix team name normalization (CSA, Ceara, etc.) so the same club maps consistently. Let me expand the alias map comprehensively for all Brazilian clubs appearing in Serie A/B/C. Let me extract and curate now.\n\nLet me get the full set of clubs in brasileirao + hist + brfootball Serie A and build aliases. Actually, let me just add a comprehensive list of aliases for Brazilian clubs based on the ALL KEYS list I saw. Let me identify the clubs that appear in the Brasileirao (the important ones for standings) and ensure each has aliases covering brasileirao (with state), hist (no state or with state), and brfootball (no state or with state suffix like \"RJ\", \"MG\" appended without hyphen).\n\nKey clubs in Brasileirao Serie A 2003-2022 that need cross-source normalization:\n- CSA (Alagoas): \"CSA\", \"CSA-AL\" → \"csa\"\n- Ceara: \"Ceara\", \"Ceara-CE\" → \"ceara\"\n- Fortaleza: \"Fortaleza\", \"Fortaleza-CE\" → \"fortaleza\" (already aliased)\n- Bahia: \"Bahia\", \"Bahia-BA\" → \"bahia\" (aliased)\n- Vitoria: \"Vitoria\", \"Vitoria-BA\" → \"vitoria_ba\" (aliased)\n- Sport: \"Sport\", \"Sport-PE\" → \"sport\" (aliased)\n- Nautico: aliased\n- Santa Cruz: \"Santa Cruz\", \"Santa Cruz-PE\" → \"santa cruz\"\n- Criciuma: aliased\n- Avai: aliased\n- Chapecoense: aliased\n- Figueirense: aliased\n- Parana: \"Parana\", \"Parana-PR\" → \"parana\" (note: I aliased \"parana\" → \"athletico_pr\"! That's WRONG — Paraná Clube is a different club from Athletico-PR. Let me fix: remove \"parana\" from athletico_pr aliases. Paraná Clube (Paraná-PR) is distinct.)\n- Atletico Goianiense: aliased\n- Goias: aliased\n- Ipatinga, America-MG, etc.\n\nLet me also handle: \"Coritiba-PR\" → \"coritiba\" (aliased), \"Atletico-MG\" (aliased), \"Athletico-PR\" (aliased), \"Botafogo-RJ\" (aliased), \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" (aliased), \"Sao Paulo-SP\" (aliased), \"Santos-SP\" (aliased), \"Palmeiras-SP\" (aliased), \"Corinthians-SP\" (aliased), \"Flamengo-RJ\" (aliased), \"Fluminense-RJ\" (aliased), \"Gremio-RS\" (aliased), \"Internacional-RS\" (aliased), \"Cruzeiro-MG\" (aliased).\n\nNow the missing ones for Serie A: CSA, Ceara, Santa Cruz, Parana, Atletico-GO (aliased), Goias (aliased), Guarani (aliased), Portuguesa (aliased), Ponte Preta (aliased), Paysandu (aliased), Juventude (aliased), Vitoria (aliased), Fortaleza (aliased), Bragantino (aliased), Cuiaba (aliased), Athletico (aliased), America-MG (aliased), Red Bull Brasil (minor).\n\nLet me add: csa, ceara, santa_cruz, parana_clube, atletico_go (have), ipatinga, juventude (have), etc. Let me check which Serie A teams from 2019 have mismatched canonical ids. Let me extract all unique teams from 2019 Brasileirao across sources and their canonical ids.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecafbfda001PLYBxkhoERpHjd","sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffeahTNKaUmDz4HW0","messageID":"msg_eecaeebcd001XyEZ5EFbGejwuO"}}
