{"type":"text","timestamp":1782087715780,"sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffeahTNKaUmDz4HW0","part":{"id":"prt_eecb4811c0014WD8QWplbLyczw","messageID":"msg_eecb4708a001FaR86Ql7oKt9l9","sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffeahTNKaUmDz4HW0","type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. All 39 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt a Brazilian Soccer MCP server in Python per `TASK.md`:\n\n**Package `brazilian_soccer_mcp/`:**\n- `normalizers.py` — team-name canonicalization (handles state suffixes, accents, full names; data-driven base/state resolution so `CSA-AL`→`csa` but `Atlético-MG`/`Atlético-GO` stay distinct), multi-format date parsing, derby list.\n- `data_loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into a unified match table, **deduplicates** overlapping sources (Brasileirão exists in 3 files; Copa do Brasil in 2), keeps extended stats separate.\n- `query_engine.py` — `QueryEngine` covering all 5 required categories (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats).\n- `mcp_server.py` — `FastMCP` server with 17 JSON tools.\n\n**Validation against spec examples:**\n- 2019 Brasileirão champion → Flamengo, 90 pts (28W 6D 4L) ✓\n- Top Brazilian player → Neymar Jr, Overall 92 ✓\n- Fla-Flu head-to-head, biggest wins, derbies, average goals ✓\n\n**Tests** (`tests/`): 39 BDD Given/When/Then-style pytest tests across normalization, match/team/player/competition/statistical queries, and the MCP server tools — all passing.","time":{"start":1782087713052,"end":1782087715779}}}
